 "overview": "The MPS School Committee is the governing body for Medford Public Schools, responsible for district policy, budget approval, and the oversight of the superintendent. Between December 2021 and October 2026, the body managed a significant shift in executive leadership, responded to critical school safety incidents, and initiated major infrastructure overhauls including a multi-year partnership with the Massachusetts School Building Authority. The committee also oversaw the adoption of new literacy curricula and addressed persistent enrollment imbalances across its elementary schools. At its most recent meetings, the body has focused on finalizing large-scale HVAC electrification projects and establishing a new community-informed strategic plan.",
